{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1357613-vtr-2e-v5-hunger-dice-and-rouse-in-vtr","id":1357613,"title":"[VtR 2e / V5] Hunger Dice and Rouse in VtR","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-29T15:18:40-08:00","id":1357613,"title":"[VtR 2e / V5] Hunger Dice and Rouse in VtR","content":"Hey all!<br /> <br /> I'm looking to mix things up for my players and how they relate to Blood in VtR, so I'm interested in trying to import the Hunger mechanics from V5. I like the lack of certainty the Hunger mechanic provides concerning how full you are and how quickly the Hunger will grow and threaten to overtake you or taint your actions.<br /> <br /> However, as usual I'm worried about some of the differences between editions and the impact that can have on the systems, especially the TN differences.<br /> <br /> I want to tie blood power growth to Potency. Right now I'm considering this: <div align=\"left\"> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 468px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blood Potency</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Rouse / Turn)</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rouse Dice</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feeding</span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blood Bags, Animals, Humans</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">2</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Animals, Humans</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Humans</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">3</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Humans slake 1 less Hunger</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Must drain &amp; kill a human to reduce Hunger &lt; 2</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Humans slake 2 less Hunger</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">etc.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">etc.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">etc.</td> </tr> </table></div> My reasoning is as follows:<ul><li>V5 scales healing ability and blood surge with Potency. I think that's a bit too much for me to convert across editions, and I prefer VtR's simpler way of keeping the ability static but increasing how much blood you can spend per turn. I think in V5 you can Rouse as much as you want per turn, whereas here I'm tying how much you can Rouse per turn to BP, just as it was in the old Blood Pool system.</li> <li>Since there's no blood pool, I need a way to simulate the greater pool or efficacy of the blood as Potency rises. I think the best way to do that is to increase the Rouse Dice so they have a greater chance of not increasing their Hunger when they rouse the blood. If I did this right, at low BP they'll become hungry a little more frequently than one Rouse die in V5, then at 2 and 3 they'll match one Rouse die in V5, then at 4 and 5 they'll be ~10% under the equivalent of two TN6 Rouse Dice.</li> <li>Getting more Rouse dice in V5 is tied to BP and only really for Disciplines at certain levels. Given the differences in the systems, and not wanting to overly track things like that, I broadened it to all Rouse checks, hoping this will help offset some of the percentage differences due to TN.</li> <li>I could keep extrapolating up to BP10, but it's not likely we'd ever reach those heights in game. In fact, I prefer a world where BP is capped at 5, with 6 reserved for diablerists only.</li> <li>Attribute/Skill max scaling is the same. It's just not really relevant to this discussion.</li> <li>When do Vampires have to feed from other Vamps. I've mulled it over, and I actually prefer V5's scale. It keeps the focus on the Vamp/Human dynamic. There's nothing STOPPING an Elder, or anyone, feeding on Kindred. In fact, the option becomes all the more appealing as it becomes less and less satisfying to feed on Humans, which I think increases the horror because it remains a choice made to sate the Hunger, rather than a necessity.</li> </ul>Any help is appreciated in refining this. Thanks! <div align=\"center\"><b>*edit* Revision 2</b></div> <br /> <br /> Ok, so after much hemming and hawing, I think I am going to try to run with this. I've made some adjustments to the scaling to ease the ramp up a bit, making it easier and more flexible at the lower levels, and increasingly more demanding to sate the Hunger as BP goes up (they can feed down to Hunger 0, for example, up until BP 3.)<br /> <br /> As for BP 6, this is a personal preference for me. Anyone else would be welcome to continue to scale this up as they like, but I prefer a scale of 5, with 6 being the special &quot;Further Beyond&quot; tier.<br /> <br /> I won't be using Messy Crits or Bestial Failures per se. This part is less nailed down right now, but I'll be looking to Atrocity Dice penalties as a guide as suggested by @Draconis.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty happy with how it turned out. ^_^ Hope it's fun for people! <div align=\"left\"> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blood Potency</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Rouse / Turn)</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rouse Dice</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feeding</span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><ul><li>Hunger Absolute Minimum: 0</li> <li>Blood Bags, Animals, Humans, Vitae</li> <li>Ways to always reduce Hunger to absolute minimum:<ul><li>Drain a human dry</li> <li>Commit diablerie</li> </ul></li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><ul><li>Blood bags slake no Hunger</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><ul><li>Animals slake no Hunger</li> <li>Hunger Minimum from feeding - Humans: 1</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><ul><li>Humans slake 1 less Hunger</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><ul><li>Hunger Minimum from feeding - Humans: 2</li> <li>Hunger Minimum from feeding - Vitae: 1</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">6</span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4</span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><ul><li>Hunger Absolute Minimum: 1</li> <li>Humans slake 2 less Hunger</li> <li>Hunger Minimum from feeding - Humans: 3</li> <li>Hunger Minimum from feeding- Vitae: 2</li> </ul></td> </tr> </table></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 02-15-2020, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T19:52:01-08:00","id":1362786,"title":"","content":"*edit: not relevant anymore*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 02-13-2020, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T13:18:22-08:00","id":1362942,"title":"","content":"V5's hunger system definitely is interesting! I liked how <i>visceral </i>and unpredictable it made the moment-to-moment existence of a vampire seem. You could be riding high, totally fine, and then five minutes and a few bad rolls later, you're starving and having to decide between whatever your goal <i>was </i>and tamping down the Beast.<br /> <br /> The idea of hiding the blood pools from the players is an interesting one. It's sort of like those videogames that don't track your ammo on the HUD, and make you count your shots yourself. If you're on the ball, there's little difference, but get distracted and it's suddenly a...&quot;Do I feel lucky, punk?&quot; situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T17:31:53-08:00","id":1362975,"title":"","content":"I feel like a Hunger type system in VTR should have Conditions involved somehow. A little less random, more of a player choice (like, resolve a Hunger condition to do something Big). I've liked the Hunger dice system, but it's a little more random than I'd prefer at times.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, that's how it works in Beast, but I don't think it would need to use that system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T18:47:19-08:00","id":1362985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1357613-vtr-2e-v5-hunger-dice-and-rouse-in-vtr?p=1362942#post1362942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5's hunger system definitely is interesting! I liked how <i>visceral </i>and unpredictable it made the moment-to-moment existence of a vampire seem. You could be riding high, totally fine, and then five minutes and a few bad rolls later, you're starving and having to decide between whatever your goal <i>was </i>and tamping down the Beast.<br /> <br /> The idea of hiding the blood pools from the players is an interesting one. It's sort of like those videogames that don't track your ammo on the HUD, and make you count your shots yourself. If you're on the ball, there's little difference, but get distracted and it's suddenly a...&quot;Do I feel lucky, punk?&quot; situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>for sure! i feel the same way about V5's Hunger and what it brings to the table. the uncertainty of it is part of the appeal, because you DON'T have control over the Hunger. it's IN you, and when it CALLS, it's hard to resist. i love that! i'm doing my best to approximate that feeling with the systems available to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like a Hunger type system in VTR should have Conditions involved somehow. A little less random, more of a player choice (like, resolve a Hunger condition to do something Big). I've liked the Hunger dice system, but it's a little more random than I'd prefer at times.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, that's how it works in Beast, but I don't think it would need to use that system.</div> </div> </div> </div>i can certainly dig what you're saying, trying to lean into the systems CofD already provides, and it does help that Beast has approached this idea of hunger as a major part of its game as well.<br /> <br /> i had a conversation with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> along these lines, and he produced an initial workup of what it could look like:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1244694-hunger-in-requiem?p=1246349#post1246349\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...49#post1246349</a><br /> <br /> \u200bI think why I'm choosing to not go with it is because i do want to keep it a little more occluded, and i don't want to have an additional Rouse die roll on top of the immediately applicable task at hand.<br /> <br /> it's a tough nut to crack, i find, a balance between a system that feels satisfying to capture the mood, but not intrusive and burdensome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 01-23-2020, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T19:08:17-08:00","id":1362988,"title":"","content":"*edit: not relevant anymore*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 02-13-2020, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T19:10:09-08:00","id":1362990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nicodemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1357613-vtr-2e-v5-hunger-dice-and-rouse-in-vtr?p=1362985#post1362985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200bI think why I'm choosing to not go with it is because i do want to keep it a little more occluded, and i don't want to have an additional Rouse die roll on top of the immediately applicable task at hand.<br /> <br /> it's a tough nut to crack, i find, a balance between a system that feels satisfying to capture the mood, but not intrusive and burdensome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the occlusion is important. One of the reasons I do like the Hunger system is because it really abstracts the amount of Vitae a character has, rather than defining it so cleanly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T08:47:26-08:00","id":1366991,"title":"","content":"Hello.<br /> We use V5\u00b4s Hunger System successfully now since almost two years in a weekly game.<br /> I would not limit rouse checks per turn. Just the action economy will limit your players enough.<br /> I did this too in the beginning and it\u00b4s not very intuitive either for players.<br /> Also - if they want to burn up their hunger in one turn: Let them! It feels good for players to maybe go &quot;All out&quot;.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, let them record their own Hunger, it will still feel <i>visceral </i>and unpredictable to them. Trust me. All my players get really itchy when their vamps reach Hunger 4. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> We use the Mending and Rolling Rousecheck with Advantage for disciplines as dictated by Blood Potency in V5.<br /> <br /> Here is my oldcomment in a tread of using hunger:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256266-hunger-pool-instead-of-hunger-dice\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256266-hunger-pool-instead-of-hunger-dice\"> Hunger pool instead of hunger dice - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256266-hunger-pool-instead-of-hunger-dice\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256266-hunger-pool-instead-of-hunger-dice </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I don&acute;t like Hunger Dice Mechanic for me They aren&acute;t giving us nothing new (Hunger frenzy was always a thing and the mechanic was better.) They are also a </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;I\u00b4m telling a story for 4 freshly embraced licks in a Requiem game WITH V5 Hunger mechanics. (When it says in Requiem to use a point of Vitae, then it\u00b4s a Rouse Check. It\u00b4s an easy hack and worked fine.)<br /> After roughly about 100+ hours of gaming it I came to certain conclusions regarding V5 Hunger.<br /> <br /> - It makes both as a player and ST the game a lot more random(fun! ^__^): The freshly embraced Ventrue clinged hard to his Humanity and declined drinking ANY blood, but was successful with EVERY rouse check after each day - which fed storywise wonderfully into his denial of his new existence! Meanwhile the Gangrel who used heavily Protean killed already a human in Hungerfrenzy and was almost always on the Edge due to almost always failing her rouse checks.<br /> - Hungerdice is both heaven and hell as a mechanic in the dicepool, especially for me as a ST.<br /> - Hunting for blood becomes way more prominent in game with V5 hunger mechanics. A vampire with Hunger 2 can quickly reach Hunger 5 by only 3 times of rousing the blood. My players get quite anxious to hunt as quickly before they reach hunger 5. Also reaching Hunger 0 is a sweet spot. Not only widens it the possible use of Blood by 20% percent(Which is a lot!) But I also homeruled that a Vampire with hunger 0 get\u00b4s +2 to resist Frenzies and +1 to rouse-the-blood-checks, also social dice penalitiey vs. mortals are reduced by 1.<br /> 2 of my players like that the other 2 don\u00b4t. - in the future I plan to use Geraukis &quot;Between the Scenes&quot; game hack to roll Hunting more into a specialized scene and into between-sessions-time.<br /> - Hunger is huge game changer regarding the power levels between younger and older vampires, just because if an elder is unlucky with it\u00b4s rouse checks, it will be on the bringe of frenzy latest after 5 rousings of the blood. (In my games I assume that most my NPC\u00b4s have about Hunger 1 or 2). On the other hand I had our Daeva in the group heal 5 levels of lethal damage without getting hungrier. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> - Rolling for Rousing of the blood are additional dice rools - that is a thing I don\u00b4t like.<br /> - I personally like that even a Vampire with Hunger 0 has this uncertainity that they don\u00b4t know how long they will last before the Beast want\u00b4s to claim them. Will it be 5 or 15 rolls? I observed it nicely in my players - which is complety on theme and mood for Vampire the Requiem with me - that it keeps Players anxious and on the edge, very much likes vampires perceive it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T10:43:24-08:00","id":1367031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1357613-vtr-2e-v5-hunger-dice-and-rouse-in-vtr?p=1366991#post1366991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello.<br /> We use V5\u00b4s Hunger System successfully now since almost two years in a weekly game.<br /> I would not limit rouse checks per turn. Just the action economy will limit your players enough.<br /> I did this too in the beginning and it\u00b4s not very intuitive either for players.<br /> Also - if they want to burn up their hunger in one turn: Let them! It feels good for players to maybe go &amp;quot;All out&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, let them record their own Hunger, it will still feel <i>visceral </i>and unpredictable to them. Trust me. All my players get really itchy when their vamps reach Hunger 4. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> We use the Mending and Rolling Rousecheck with Advantage for disciplines as dictated by Blood Potency in V5.<br /> <br /> Here is my oldcomment in a tread of using hunger:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256266-hunger-pool-instead-of-hunger-dice\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256266-hunger-pool-instead-of-hunger-dice\"> Hunger pool instead of hunger dice - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256266-hunger-pool-instead-of-hunger-dice\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256266-hunger-pool-instead-of-hunger-dice </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I don&acute;t like Hunger Dice Mechanic for me They aren&acute;t giving us nothing new (Hunger frenzy was always a thing and the mechanic was better.) They are also a </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &amp;quot;I\u00b4m telling a story for 4 freshly embraced licks in a Requiem game WITH V5 Hunger mechanics. (When it says in Requiem to use a point of Vitae, then it\u00b4s a Rouse Check. It\u00b4s an easy hack and worked fine.)<br /> After roughly about 100+ hours of gaming it I came to certain conclusions regarding V5 Hunger.<br /> <br /> - It makes both as a player and ST the game a lot more random(fun! ^__^): The freshly embraced Ventrue clinged hard to his Humanity and declined drinking ANY blood, but was successful with EVERY rouse check after each day - which fed storywise wonderfully into his denial of his new existence! Meanwhile the Gangrel who used heavily Protean killed already a human in Hungerfrenzy and was almost always on the Edge due to almost always failing her rouse checks.<br /> - Hungerdice is both heaven and hell as a mechanic in the dicepool, especially for me as a ST.<br /> - Hunting for blood becomes way more prominent in game with V5 hunger mechanics. A vampire with Hunger 2 can quickly reach Hunger 5 by only 3 times of rousing the blood. My players get quite anxious to hunt as quickly before they reach hunger 5. Also reaching Hunger 0 is a sweet spot. Not only widens it the possible use of Blood by 20% percent(Which is a lot!) But I also homeruled that a Vampire with hunger 0 get\u00b4s +2 to resist Frenzies and +1 to rouse-the-blood-checks, also social dice penalitiey vs. mortals are reduced by 1.<br /> 2 of my players like that the other 2 don\u00b4t. - in the future I plan to use Geraukis &amp;quot;Between the Scenes&amp;quot; game hack to roll Hunting more into a specialized scene and into between-sessions-time.<br /> - Hunger is huge game changer regarding the power levels between younger and older vampires, just because if an elder is unlucky with it\u00b4s rouse checks, it will be on the bringe of frenzy latest after 5 rousings of the blood. (In my games I assume that most my NPC\u00b4s have about Hunger 1 or 2). On the other hand I had our Daeva in the group heal 5 levels of lethal damage without getting hungrier. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> - Rolling for Rousing of the blood are additional dice rools - that is a thing I don\u00b4t like.<br /> - I personally like that even a Vampire with Hunger 0 has this uncertainity that they don\u00b4t know how long they will last before the Beast want\u00b4s to claim them. Will it be 5 or 15 rolls? I observed it nicely in my players - which is complety on theme and mood for Vampire the Requiem with me - that it keeps Players anxious and on the edge, very much likes vampires perceive it.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of great information, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T16:19:23-08:00","id":1367117,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1305_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1305\" data-vbnamecard=\"1305\">maekkel</a> thanks for sharing!<br /> <br /> did you not run into any issues mixing the healing of V5 with the damage system of VtR? or with the target number for success difference when Rousing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 02-11-2020, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T07:31:38-08:00","id":1368040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nicodemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1357613-vtr-2e-v5-hunger-dice-and-rouse-in-vtr?p=1367117#post1367117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1305_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1305\" data-vbnamecard=\"1305\">maekkel</a> thanks for sharing!<br /> <br /> did you not run into any issues mixing the healing of V5 with the damage system of VtR? or with the target number for success difference when Rousing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Grateful to serve!<br /> <br /> No, actually not but we use also a slightly changed system. Also we rarely have combat, as most of my players avoid it.<br /> Also Adversaries will normally not attack with heavy weaponry like swords or chainsaws or assault rifles. <br /> Thus a normal attack does mostly suxx+weapon mod in damage per attack, which means 1 to 7+ damage per hit. and afterwards the damage is halved.<br /> As the average vampire has 7-8 healthlevels, this hardly kills them.<br /> <br /> We use 3 damage types plus eventual tilts:<br /> Combat is Dicepool VS Dicepool - who makes more successes, hits.<br /> <br /> <b>light damage</b> is always halved, rounded down = sources: brawl, melee, firearms :<br /> Mending like in V5 , but each rouse check heals at least 2 levels<br /> <b>heavy damage</b> is always halved except for banes = sources: some supernatural weaponry, some banes, a vampire receiving more light damage than she got health levels :<br /> Mending like in V5 , for agravated = 1 Level is healed for 1 rouse check<br /> <b>supernatural/aggravated</b> damage (never halved) = sources: banes, extreme damage<br /> Mending: only once a night possible and 1 level costs +1 Hunger + 1 rouse check and 1 WP.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}